WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.106
The patronage machine.

00:00:02.056 --> 00:00:05.420
Over three thousand Governor-in-Council appointments.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.215
Half a billion dollars annually in salaries and benefits.

00:00:09.215 --> 00:00:12.818
Zero mandatory merit criteria for most positions.

00:00:12.818 --> 00:00:16.295
This is how Canada's government rewards its allies.

00:00:16.295 --> 00:00:22.727
Three hundred and thirty federal judges appointed by Trudeau between 2015 and 2025.

00:00:22.727 --> 00:00:27.340
Every single one selected through a process controlled by the Prime Minister's Office.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.374
The diversity statistics look good on paper.

00:00:30.374 --> 00:00:33.568
The accountability mechanism is nonexistent.

00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:35.477
The Senate of Canada.

00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:37.999
One hundred and five senators.

00:00:37.999 --> 00:00:39.602
All appointed.

00:00:39.602 --> 00:00:41.363
Zero elected.

00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:46.579
Ninety-seven percent of Independent Senate Group votes aligned with the government in their first term.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.863
Independent in name only.

00:00:48.863 --> 00:00:51.136
Crown corporation boards.

00:00:51.136 --> 00:00:55.772
The directors who oversee billions in public spending are selected through patronage.

00:00:55.772 --> 00:00:57.909
No competitive hiring.

00:00:57.909 --> 00:01:00.159
No public accountability.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:05.693
The people who are supposed to watch the money... are the same people who got their jobs as political favours.

00:01:05.693 --> 00:01:08.431
The Director of Public Prosecutions.

00:01:08.431 --> 00:01:10.397
Seven-year terms.

00:01:10.397 --> 00:01:14.602
Appointed by Governor-in-Council on the Attorney General's recommendation.

00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:20.295
The person who decides which cases to prosecute is selected by the people most likely to be prosecuted.

00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:21.977
Think about that.

00:01:21.977 --> 00:01:27.159
Zero remedies ordered for whistleblowers under the Public Servants Disclosure Protection Act.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:29.136
In eighteen years.

00:01:29.136 --> 00:01:30.659
Not one.

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:33.636
The act was designed to look like protection.

00:01:33.636 --> 00:01:36.511
It was designed to function as containment.

00:01:36.511 --> 00:01:39.579
Two Ethics Commissioner findings against Trudeau.

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:42.556
Finding number one and finding number two.

00:01:42.556 --> 00:01:45.056
Zero criminal consequences.

00:01:45.056 --> 00:01:47.602
The Ethics Commissioner can find.

00:01:47.602 --> 00:01:50.454
The Ethics Commissioner cannot enforce.

00:01:50.454 --> 00:01:52.590
That is not oversight.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.272
That is theatre.
